-q
----------------------------------------------------------------------
10 CLS
' COS gives the cosine of the argument in radians, see 5.1.3. The result is
' always Single and lies between -1 and 1. The constant is folded by the
' compiler, the variable goes through the FCOS runtime call, both ways have
' to give the same result.
' A Single keeps about 7 digits, so every check uses a tolerance. Every line
' prints the expected value, the calculated one, and -1 if they match.
20 A = COS(0)
25 E% = ABS(A - 1.0) < 0.00001
30 PRINT "1"; A; E%
35 F = 0.0
40 A = COS(F)
45 E% = ABS(A - 1.0) < 0.00001
50 PRINT "1"; A; E%
' The cosine of PI/3 is 0.5, of PI/4 is the half of the root of 2
55 A = COS(PI/3)
60 E% = ABS(A - 0.5) < 0.00001
65 PRINT ".5"; A; E%
70 F = PI/3
75 A = COS(F)
80 E% = ABS(A - 0.5) < 0.00001
85 PRINT ".5"; A; E%
90 A = COS(PI/4)
95 E% = ABS(A - 0.7071068) < 0.00001
100 PRINT ".7071068"; A; E%
' The cosine is 0 at PI/2 and -1 at PI. The runtime calculates it with a
' polynomial, so at the very bottom the result can be off by the last digit
' and come out slightly below -1; the bound below allows for that.
120 A = COS(PI/2)
125 E% = ABS(A) < 0.0001
130 PRINT "0"; A; E%
135 F = PI/2
140 A = COS(F)
145 E% = ABS(A) < 0.0001
150 PRINT "0"; A; E%
155 A = COS(PI)
160 E% = ABS(A + 1.0) < 0.00001 AND A >= -1.000001
165 PRINT "-1"; A; E%
' The cosine of 1 radian
170 A = COS(1)
175 E% = ABS(A - 0.5403023) < 0.00001
180 PRINT ".5403023"; A; E%
185 F = 1.0
190 A = COS(F)
195 E% = ABS(A - 0.5403023) < 0.00001
200 PRINT ".5403023"; A; E%
' COS is an even function, so a negative argument gives the same result
205 B% = 1
210 A = COS(B%)
215 E% = ABS(A - 0.5403023) < 0.00001
220 PRINT ".5403023"; A; E%
225 B% = -1
230 A = COS(B%)
235 E% = ABS(A - 0.5403023) < 0.00001
240 PRINT ".5403023"; A; E%
' The cosine of the other arguments
245 A = COS(0.5)
250 E% = ABS(A - 0.8775826) < 0.00001
255 PRINT ".8775826"; A; E%
260 F = 0.5
265 A = COS(F)
270 E% = ABS(A - 0.8775826) < 0.00001
275 PRINT ".8775826"; A; E%
' Between PI/2 and 3*PI/2 the cosine is negative
280 A = COS(2)
285 E% = ABS(A + 0.4161468) < 0.00001
290 PRINT "-.4161468"; A; E%
295 A = COS(3)
300 E% = ABS(A + 0.9899925) < 0.00001
305 PRINT "-.9899925"; A; E%
' COS(-X) = COS(X), see 5.1.3
310 F = 0.7
315 A = COS(-F) - COS(F)
320 E% = ABS(A) < 0.00001
325 PRINT "0"; A; E%
' SIN(X)^2 + COS(X)^2 is 1 for any X
330 A = COS(F) * COS(F) + SIN(F) * SIN(F)
335 E% = ABS(A - 1.0) < 0.0001
340 PRINT "1"; A; E%
' COS(2X) is 1 - 2 * SIN(X)^2
345 A = COS(F + F) - 1.0 + 2.0 * SIN(F) * SIN(F)
350 E% = ABS(A) < 0.0001
355 PRINT "0"; A; E%
' The argument is an expression
360 F = 1.0
365 A = COS(F + F)
370 E% = ABS(A + 0.4161468) < 0.00001
375 PRINT "-.4161468"; A; E%
